  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 91036662a85844eb162bdfbe2ea8ce9c, type: 3}
  m_Name: BrazilianRules
  m_EditorClassIdentifier:
  displayName: Brazilian
  description: International draughts on a smaller 8x8 board - flying kings, mandatory maximum capture.
  longDescription: "<b>Basic Movement</b>\nDark Squares Only: pieces move diagonally on the 32 dark squares. Forward Only: regular pieces can only step one square diagonally forward.\n\n<b>Capture Mechanics</b>\nBackward Captures: regular pieces can jump backward to capture, though they can't step backward normally. Mandatory Maximum: capturing is mandatory, and if you have multiple jumping paths, you must choose the one that captures the most pieces. King Priority: if two different paths capture the exact same number of pieces, you must choose the path that captures more Kings. The No-Removal Rule: captured pieces stay on the board until the entire multi-jump turn is complete - you can't jump over the same piece twice.\n\n<b>The Flying King</b>\nEnd-of-Turn Promotion: a piece only becomes a king if it finishes its turn on the opponent's back row - if it jumps through the back row and lands elsewhere, it does not promote. Long-Range Flight: a king can slide any number of empty squares along a diagonal line. Long-Range Jumps: a king can capture an enemy piece from a distance, fly over it, and choose which empty square to land on behind it.\n\n<b>Winning the Game</b>\nElimination or Blockade: you win by capturing all opposing pieces or trapping your opponent so they have no legal moves left."
  rows: 8
  columns: 8
  pieceRowsPerSide: 3
  movementScheme: 0
  piecesOnAllSquares: 0
  leaveBackRowEmpty: 0
  flyingKings: 1
  menCaptureBackward: 1
  menCannotCaptureKings: 0
  mustCaptureMaximum: 1
  preferKingMover: 0
  preferKingCaptures: 1
  preferEarlierKingCapture: 0
  midChainPromotionRule: 0
  deferCaptureRemoval: 1
  forbidImmediateReversal: 0
  noProgressMoveLimit: 25
  singleManLosesToKing: 0
